.TH FORMATUSB 1 "2026-07-20" "MX Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
formatusb \- format removable USB devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B formatusb
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B formatusb
is a graphical utility for formatting removable USB devices. Select a target device, a filesystem type, and optionally a filesystem label. By default the complete device is repartitioned with one partition before it is formatted.
.PP
The supported filesystem choices include FAT32/VFAT, NTFS, ext4, and exFAT. The partition-table choice can be MBR/msdos, GPT, or automatic. Devices smaller than 2 TiB use MBR/msdos by default when automatic selection is used.
.PP
Enable
.B Show Partitions
when the operation should target an individual partition instead of repartitioning the complete device. Enable
.B Show All Devices
to remove the removable-device filter.
.PP
Formatting destroys data on the selected device or partition. Check the target carefully before confirming.
.SH OPTIONS
This application has no documented command-line options. The graphical interface provides all operations.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/formatusb
Installed HTML help, license, and changelog documentation.
.SH AUTHOR
MX Linux contributors.
